From 3a2e51006f31d8b2376e964971ecddfa3e60ac81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yashika <yashika@fedev.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Strategy Arena: intraday strategies competing with
 simulated money

Several intraday strategies paper-trade the same stocks on the same
5-minute bars, each with its own copy of the daily capital, so the
leaderboard shows which one actually makes money after costs.

- arena/strategies.py: ORB, VWAP reclaim, EMA 9/21, RSI bounce, Bollinger
  volume breakout, the original 4-signal score, and a buy-at-open
  benchmark. Causal indicators only (no lookahead).
- arena/costs.py: brokerage, STT, exchange, SEBI, stamp duty, GST and
  slippage on every leg.
- arena/engine.py: pessimistic fills (stop wins ties, gaps fill at open),
  risk-based sizing, daily loss limit, 14:45 entry cutoff, 15:15
  square-off, end-of-day settlement, benching losers into shadow mode
  and reinstating them on evidence. Same code path for live and replay.
- arena/service.py + scheduler: opens/advances/settles each session,
  catches up a day the server slept through; network fetched outside
  the store lock.
- API: /api/arena (view, config, reset, bench/reinstate, trades,
  backtest over the last 10-60 sessions).
- Frontend: Arena tab (desktop: header button) with leaderboard,
  per-strategy trades, backtest and settings.
- 15 new tests; full suite 138 passing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
